entityDescription:
The Lithuanian Non-Formal Education Agency (LINE&Scaron;A) (until 1 September 2023 &ndash; the Lithuanian Centre for Non-Formal Education of Students) is a budgetary institution subordinate to the Ministry of Education, Science and Sports, providing assistance in the implementation of state policy in the areas of non-formal education of children and vocational guidance (career education).
LINE&Scaron;A tasks:
- to develop the system of non-formal education for children;
- to organize, within its competence, information and qualification improvement of participants in the education system;
- to coordinate and carry out vocational guidance for students;
- to create and develop a STEAM education ecosystem;
- to create conditions for the talents and creativity of highly motivated students to unfold and to ensure students' participation in international events.
